From 05d93b342b20d9bbe13960e6611aac5bad84fbc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:39:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(flowchart): crowded heads keep apart; advance heads
 face a short last leg; Metrics non-exhaustive (B1 review r3 #4-#6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Report §2.3 (Q1+M1).

#4 An over-full side takes its ports about 10 px apart, and the 11 px
head turned their heads into one saw-tooth band (x2_fan's Sink: six
heads at a 10.3 px pitch). crowded_heads finds arrowheads standing side
by side (parallel within 10 deg, tips level along the heading, 1+ px
apart across it) closer than a head and HEAD_GAP (1.5 px), and paints
them narrower — the pitch less the gap, to the half px, never under
HEAD_MIN_WIDTH (6 px) nor too narrow to cover the stroke where the
painter cuts it (a wide linkStyle stroke keeps its whole head) — in
an `<base>-w<width>` marker (`arrow-w8_5`; marker_def_sized). Heads
with room keep #arrow; heads sharing a port are left alone. Painter-only.
Corpus: 3 heads in bench-75 static (x2_fan 6, x5-close 4, x6 4 among
the extra inputs). The ports stage spreading such ends (report §2.4)
stays the real fix.

#5 polyline_d_painted (advance painter): a last leg shorter than the
cut and SQUARE_END_ENTRY ended the stroke on the leg before it, and
orient="auto" tilted the head. Now the route is kept up to that far
back, runs straight to that point on the last leg's line and on along
it, so the stroke ends a cut short of the tip heading along the last
leg (the advance examples' stubs are 18 px or more: no output change).

#6 quality::Metrics::end_kink's doc rewrapped under 100 columns.
Metrics becomes #[non_exhaustive]: its phase-B columns (end_tilt …
x_drawn, end_kink) already broke struct literals outside the crate in
this release; read its fields or start from Metrics::default() (in
CHANGELOG under Breaking). New columns no longer break it.

Tests: crowded_heads_narrow_so_neighbours_keep_apart (half of each head
and the gap fit in the pitch; a head with room stays whole; the floor
holds; the SVG uses both markers),
an_advance_route_with_a_short_last_leg_keeps_its_head_on_that_leg.
No snapshot or gate changed. README: the arrow-w marker.

